    "created_at": "2016-07-06T15:21:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-06T15:21:24Z",
    "body": "The spec actually says \"fully opaque black\", not \"transparent black\" so if Edge uses transparent black, then it is neither spec compliant nor compatible with other browsers.  \n\nThe wording in the spec used to be different and did not reference the notion of \"being rendered\" : \"If the computed value of the 'color' property is undefined for a particular case (e.g. because the element is not in a document), then the \"computed value of the 'color' property\" for the purposes of determining the computed value of the <code\n  title=\"\">currentColor</code> keyword is fully opaque black.\"\n\nThe change comes from:\ncommit 285b52f213855dffbc6185ead6f26baa9ce9059f\nAuthor: Ian Hickson ian@hixie.ch\nDate:   Fri Nov 16 20:26:07 2012 +0000\n    [agiow](0) First draft of a way to do canvas in workers.\n\nI am pretty sure this change did not intend to modify pre-existing behavior and that the objective was to cover the case of a rendering context that lives in a Worker (where style computation is not possible).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/230805794/reactions",
